new_lessons += [
L('secrets-engines', 'KV Engine Deep Dive: v1 vs v2 Operations',
 ["kv-v2 versions every write and keeps max-versions history; delete is soft (undelete restores), destroy is permanent, and metadata/ tracks versions independently of data/.",
  "Policy paths differ: kv-v2 requires secret/data/app for reads, secret/metadata/app for version management, secret/destroy/app and secret/undelete/app for lifecycle \u2014 the number-one policy bug is writing kv-v1 paths against a v2 mount.",
  "Check-and-set (CAS): pass cas=<version> on write to make concurrent writers safe; a stale CAS fails instead of silently overwriting.",
  "Tune per mount: max-versions, cas-required, delete-version-after. Set delete-version-after for compliance auto-expiry of old versions."],
 "vault kv put -mount=secret app/db password=s3cret\nvault kv get -version=2 -mount=secret app/db\n# policy needs: secret/data/app/db (read), secret/metadata/app/db (list)",
 "kv-v2 policies copied from kv-v1 examples fail closed with 'permission denied' \u2014 always include the /data/ path.",
 ["Enabling kv-v2 on an existing v1 mount path without migrating data expectations \u2014 versioning changes delete semantics.",
  "Granting secret/app/* instead of secret/data/app/*: looks right, denies everything on v2.",
  "Ignoring max-versions: unbounded history grows storage and leaks old secrets past rotation."],
 "Mount a kv-v2 engine, write three versions, soft-delete, then undelete version 2."),

L('secrets-engines', 'Cubbyhole and Response Wrapping',
 ["Cubbyhole is a per-token KV that dies with the token: perfect for bootstrapping (drop the AppRole secret-id in cubbyhole, hand the wrapping token to the app).",
  "Response wrapping: Vault returns a single-use wrapping token instead of the secret; the recipient unwraps within the TTL. The secret never sits in logs, CI output, or chat.",
  "Wrapping works on any response: vault kv get -wrap-ttl=60s, or wrap an AppRole secret-id. TTLs are short (minutes) \u2014 wrapping is a delivery mechanism, not storage.",
  "Audit still records that a wrap happened (request path, no secret bytes) \u2014 you get delivery proof without secret exposure."],
 "vault kv get -wrap-ttl=120 -mount=secret app/db   # returns wrapping_token, not the secret\nvault unwrap <wrapping_token>                      # single use, then it is gone",
 "Wrap a KV read, then unwrap it; observe the audit log shows the wrap but not the value.",
 ["Wrapping with a 24h TTL: long-lived wrapping tokens are just secrets with extra steps.",
  "Unwrapping twice: the token is single-use; the second unwrap fails and the secret must be re-wrapped.",
  "Using cubbyhole for durable storage: it evaporates with the token \u2014 it is a mailbox, not a vault."],
 "Deliver a secret to a teammate using only a wrapping token; verify they cannot unwrap twice."),

L('secrets-engines', 'Lease Mechanics and Revocation',
 ["Every dynamic secret and service token carries a lease: TTL, max TTL, renewable flag. Expiry is enforced server-side; clients must renew or re-request.",
  "Renewal: vault lease renew extends within max TTL. Apps should renew at ~2/3 of TTL and handle renewal failure by re-authenticating \u2014 the standard agent/sidecar pattern.",
  "Revocation: vault lease revoke kills one lease; revoke-prefix kills a subtree (e.g., all creds from database/creds/). Revocation is the incident-response kill switch.",
  "Lease storms: thousands of clients renewing on the same schedule thundering-herd the leader. Jitter renewal and stagger TTLs."],
 "vault lease renew database/creds/orders-role/abc123\nvault lease revoke -prefix=database/creds/orders-role   # kill switch",
 "Revoke a lease prefix and watch the app fail closed; then fix the app to re-request on 403.",
 ["Setting TTLs longer than the rotation policy requires: the lease IS the rotation interval.",
  "Non-renewable tokens for long-lived services: they expire and the 3 AM page is yours.",
  "revoke-prefix typos: a wrong prefix revokes the wrong subtree \u2014 dry-run with lease lookup first."],
 "Issue a 5-minute dynamic credential, renew it once, then revoke-prefix and observe."),

L('secrets-engines', 'Mount Tuning and Engine Options',
 ["vault secrets tune sets per-mount default TTL, max TTL, and listing visibility; tune the mount, not every role, so policy stays DRY.",
  "default-lease-ttl and max-lease-ttl on the mount bound every credential issued there \u2014 the mount is the guardrail, roles are the refinement.",
  "Move and remount: vault secrets move relocates a mount's data to a new path; plan path layouts (secret/, transit/, pki/) before production data lands.",
  "Disable with care: vault secrets disable destroys the mount AND its data. There is no undo \u2014 snapshot first, every time."],
 "vault secrets tune -default-lease-ttl=1h -max-lease-ttl=24h secret/\nvault secrets move secret/ secret-v1-archived/",
 "Tune a mount's TTLs, issue a credential, and confirm the lease honors the mount bounds.",
 ["Tuning max-lease-ttl DOWN on a mount with outstanding long leases: existing leases keep old TTLs, new ones clamp \u2014 know which you are testing.",
  "Disabling a mount to 'clean up' in prod: data loss. Snapshot, verify, then disable.",
  "Forgetting listing-visibility: tune it so UIs do not leak mount names to low-privilege tokens."],
 "Snapshot, then practice a secrets move on a scratch mount."),
]

